Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T00:10:58Z","closed_at":"2025-06-11T23:22:34Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107426","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107426","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107426.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107426.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-11T23:22:34Z"},"body":"- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107294\r\n\r\nThe line is now clamped to prevent the error.\r\nI also did it to warning start and end lines since this could also happen with warnings, like a Line 1 UNTYPED_DECLARATION warning gives an error for line -1.\r\n\r\nI also fixed some edge cases in the warning highlighting logic.\r\nIf only the end of a warning is folded, the start of it is now still highlighted. This can happen with a missing tool warning and a function at the end of the file.\r\nIf only the start of the warning is folded, the end is highlighted as well as now the folded line. This can happen with a multiline string that isn't indented.\r\nThe last line of a multiple line highlight is now highlighted, since it is should be considered inclusive. This can be seen with multiline strings and untyped functions.\r\n\r\n`get_folded_line_header` returns the same line if it is already unfolded, so I also simplified the logic a bit.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.co